      "Bash(git commit -m \"$\\(cat <<''EOF''\nAdd environment variable support for sensitive configuration values\n\nImplement secure configuration management by allowing sensitive values \\(tokens, passwords, API keys\\) to be stored in environment variables instead of directly in config.yaml files.\n\nChanges:\n- Updated schema.py to make sensitive fields optional \\(plex.token, auth.password, auth.secret_key, trakt.client_id\\)\n- Added _apply_env_overrides\\(\\) to loader.py to read and validate environment variables\n- Created .env.example with documentation for all supported variables\n- Updated .gitignore to exclude .env files from version control\n- Updated docker-compose.yml to reference environment variables from .env file\n- Updated example.config.yaml with security best practices and auth section\n- Updated README.md with comprehensive security documentation and Docker integration guide\n\nSupported environment variables:\n- HSH_PLEX_TOKEN: Plex authentication token\n- HSH_AUTH_PASSWORD: Authentication password \\(when auth enabled\\)\n- HSH_AUTH_SECRET_KEY: JWT secret key \\(when auth enabled\\)\n- HSH_TRAKT_CLIENT_ID: Trakt API client ID \\(when Trakt enabled\\)\n\nEnvironment variables take precedence over config.yaml values. This change is backward compatible - existing configs with secrets in YAML continue to work.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code]\\(https://claude.com/claude-code\\)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n\\)\")",
